{"ref":"BDB, סֹ֫בֶל","hw":"סֹ֫בֶל","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">סֹ֫בֶל</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Isaiah 10:27\" href=\"/Isaiah.10.27\">Is 10:27</a></sup> <strong>burden</strong> (always fig. of burden of tyranny);—only sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">סֻבֳּלוֹ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 10:27\" href=\"/Isaiah.10.27\">Is 10:27</a> (v. reff. on <span dir=\"rtl\">סֻבְּכוֹ</span>, [<span dir=\"rtl\">סְבֹךְ</span>]), <span dir=\"rtl\">עֹל ס׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 9:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.9.3\">9:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 14:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.14.25\">14:25</a> (in all conceived as burden resting on shoulders).","next":"BDB, סַבָּל","prev":"BDB, סֵ֫בֶל"}